#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/texture_blit_shader.rst:6
msgid "Texture blit shaders are used to define the behavior of blit calls on a :ref:`DrawableTexture2D <doc_drawable_textures>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/texture_blit_shader.rst:9
msgid "Texture blit shaders only have one processing function, the ``blit()`` function, which runs for every pixel of the source texture inside the rect given to ``blit_rect()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/texture_blit_shader.rst:15
msgid "See :ref:`doc_drawable_textures` for more information on how to use texture blit shaders as part of a DrawableTexture."
msgstr ""

